# ABP Application Layer Patterns

> **Docs**: https://abp.io/docs/latest/framework/architecture/domain-driven-design/application-services

## Application Service Structure

### Interface (Application.Contracts)
```csharp
public interface ITraineeAppService : IApplicationService
{
    Task<TraineeDto> GetAsync(Guid id);
    Task<PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>> GetListAsync(GetTraineeListInput input);
    Task<TraineeDto> CreateAsync(CreateUpdateTraineeDto input);
    Task<TraineeDto> UpdateAsync(Guid id, CreateUpdateTraineeDto input);
    Task DeleteAsync(Guid id);
}
```

### Implementation (Application) — fat service, generic repository, Mapster
The AppService is **fat**: it injects the **generic `IRepository<T, Guid>`**, does its own
querying inline, runs cross-aggregate checks, and maps out with `ObjectMapper` (Mapster). It
does NOT delegate to a per-entity `Manager`/`Mapper` for simple CRUD.

```csharp
[Authorize(CoachAppPermissions.Trainees.Default)]
public class TraineeAppService : CoachAppAppService, ITraineeAppService
{
    private readonly IRepository<Trainee, Guid> _traineeRepository;

    public TraineeAppService(IRepository<Trainee, Guid> traineeRepository)
        => _traineeRepository = traineeRepository;

    public virtual async Task<TraineeDto> GetAsync(Guid id)
    {
        var trainee = await _traineeRepository.GetAsync(id);
        return ObjectMapper.Map<Trainee, TraineeDto>(trainee);
    }

    public virtual async Task<PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>> GetListAsync(GetTraineeListInput input)
    {
        var query = await _traineeRepository.GetQueryableAsync();
        query = query
            .WhereIf(!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input.Filter), x => x.Code.Contains(input.Filter!))
            .WhereIf(input.IsActive.HasValue, x => x.IsActive == input.IsActive!.Value);

        var totalCount = await AsyncExecuter.CountAsync(query);
        var sorting = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input.Sorting) ? $"{nameof(Trainee.Code)} asc" : input.Sorting;
        var trainees = await AsyncExecuter.ToListAsync(
            query.OrderBy(sorting).Skip(input.SkipCount).Take(input.MaxResultCount)); // System.Linq.Dynamic.Core

        return new PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>(
            totalCount, ObjectMapper.Map<List<Trainee>, List<TraineeDto>>(trainees));
    }

    [Authorize(CoachAppPermissions.Trainees.Create)]
    public virtual async Task<TraineeDto> CreateAsync(CreateUpdateTraineeDto input)
    {
        await CheckCodeDuplicationAsync(input.Code); // cross-aggregate uniqueness — needs the repo
        var trainee = Trainee.Create(GuidGenerator.Create(), input.Code, input.FirstName, CurrentTenant.Id);
        await _traineeRepository.InsertAsync(trainee, autoSave: true);
        return ObjectMapper.Map<Trainee, TraineeDto>(trainee);
    }

    [Authorize(CoachAppPermissions.Trainees.Update)]
    public virtual async Task<TraineeDto> UpdateAsync(Guid id, CreateUpdateTraineeDto input)
    {
        var trainee = await _traineeRepository.GetAsync(id);
        await CheckCodeDuplicationAsync(input.Code, id);
        trainee.Code = input.Code;            // public setter for plain fields
        trainee.FirstName = input.FirstName;
        // trainee.SetSchedule(...) for guarded invariants
        await _traineeRepository.UpdateAsync(trainee, autoSave: true);
        return ObjectMapper.Map<Trainee, TraineeDto>(trainee);
    }

    protected virtual async Task CheckCodeDuplicationAsync(string code, Guid? excludedId = null)
    {
        var existing = await _traineeRepository.FirstOrDefaultAsync(x => x.Code == code);
        if (existing != null && existing.Id != excludedId)
        {
            throw new BusinessException(CoachAppDomainErrorCodes.TraineeCodeAlreadyExists)
                .WithData("Code", code);
        }
    }
}
```

## Application Service Best Practices
- Don't repeat entity name in method names (`GetAsync` not `GetTraineeAsync`)
- Accept/return DTOs only, never entities
- ID not inside the Create/Update DTO - pass separately
- **Fat service**: inject the generic `IRepository<T, Guid>` and do querying inline
  (`GetQueryableAsync`, `WhereIf`, `System.Linq.Dynamic.Core` `.OrderBy(sorting)`, `.Skip().Take()`,
  `AsyncExecuter`). Add a custom repository only for a genuinely complex, reused query.
- Put cross-aggregate uniqueness/existence checks here (they need the repo), throwing
  `BusinessException(CoachAppDomainErrorCodes.X)`; single-aggregate invariants stay on the entity.
- Call `UpdateAsync` explicitly (don't assume change tracking); use `autoSave: true` on write.
- Cross-feature reads are fine: call the other feature's app service, or inject its generic
  `IRepository<T, Guid>` for an existence check.
- Don't use `IFormFile`/`Stream` - pass `byte[]` from controllers
- Use base class properties (`Clock`, `CurrentUser`, `GuidGenerator`, `L`) instead of injecting these services

## DTO Naming Conventions

| Purpose | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| List query input | `Get{Entity}ListInput` | `GetTraineeListInput` |
| Create + update input | `CreateUpdate{Entity}Dto` | `CreateUpdateTraineeDto` |
| Single entity output | `{Entity}Dto` | `TraineeDto` |

CoachApp uses **one combined `CreateUpdate{Entity}Dto`** for both create and update (mirroring
`CreateUpdateTraineeDto`). Split into separate `Create`/`Update` DTOs only when the two shapes
genuinely diverge. Output DTOs derive from `FullAuditedEntityDto<Guid>`.

## DTO Location
- Define DTOs in `CoachApp.Application.Contracts` under `Entites/<Feature>/`
  (namespace `CoachApp.Entites.<Feature>`), alongside `I<Entity>AppService`.
- This allows sharing with clients (HttpApi.Client, generated proxies).

## Validation

Input validation is **DataAnnotations on the DTO** (the primary and default mechanism). Source
string lengths from `<Entity>Consts` so the DTO, entity and EF config never drift.

> **Do NOT use FluentValidation** in CoachApp. Input format/required-field checks = DataAnnotations;
> business invariants = `Check.*` + `BusinessException` in the entity (or the fat AppService when
> the rule needs the repository).

### Data Annotations
```csharp
public class CreateUpdateTraineeDto
{
    [Required]
    [StringLength(TraineeConsts.MaxCodeLength)]
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required]
    [StringLength(TraineeConsts.MaxFirstNameLength)]
    public string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [EmailAddress]
    [StringLength(TraineeConsts.MaxEmailLength)]
    public string? Email { get; set; }

    public bool IsActive { get; set; } = true;
}
```

### Custom Validation with IValidatableObject
Before adding custom validation, decide if it's a **domain rule** or **application rule**:
- **Domain rule**: Put validation in the entity's `static Create`/behavior method (enforces invariants),
  or in the fat AppService when it needs the repository (cross-aggregate).
- **Application rule**: Use DTO DataAnnotations (input format, required fields).

Only use `IValidatableObject` for application-level validation that can't be expressed with data annotations:

```csharp
public class CreateUpdateTraineeDto : IValidatableObject
{
    public string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string LastName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public IEnumerable<ValidationResult> Validate(ValidationContext validationContext)
    {
        if (FirstName == LastName)
        {
            yield return new ValidationResult(
                "FirstName and LastName cannot be the same!",
                new[] { nameof(FirstName), nameof(LastName) }
            );
        }
    }
}
```

## Error Handling

### Business Exceptions
Use a constant from `CoachAppDomainErrorCodes` (`"CoachApp:0000N"`), mapped to a localization key:
```csharp
throw new BusinessException(CoachAppDomainErrorCodes.TraineeCodeAlreadyExists)
    .WithData("Code", code);
```

### Entity Not Found
`IRepository.GetAsync(id)` already throws `EntityNotFoundException` when missing — you rarely
need to check explicitly. Use `FindAsync` only when a null result is a valid path:
```csharp
var trainee = await _traineeRepository.FindAsync(id);
if (trainee == null)
{
    throw new EntityNotFoundException(typeof(Trainee), id);
}
```

### User-Friendly Exceptions
```csharp
throw new UserFriendlyException(L["TraineeNotAvailable"]);
```

### HTTP Status Code Mapping
Status code mapping is **configurable** in ABP (do not rely on a fixed mapping in business logic).

| Exception | Typical HTTP Status |
|-----------|-------------|
| `AbpValidationException` | 400 |
| `AbpAuthorizationException` | 401/403 |
| `EntityNotFoundException` | 404 |
| `BusinessException` | 403 (but configurable) |
| Other exceptions | 500 |

## Auto API Controllers
ABP automatically generates API controllers for application services:
- Interface must inherit `IApplicationService` (which already has `[RemoteService]` attribute)
- HTTP methods determined by method name prefix (Get, Create, Update, Delete)
- Use `[RemoteService(false)]` to disable auto API generation for specific methods

## Object Mapping (Mapster)
CoachApp uses **Mapster** — NOT Mapperly, NOT AutoMapper. Do not add `[Mapper]`/`MapperBase`
(Mapperly), `CreateMap`/`Profile` (AutoMapper), or scatter `.Adapt<T>()` calls in services.
Always map through ABP's `ObjectMapper.Map<TSource, TDestination>()`.

### Central config
All mappings live in one place — `CoachAppMapsterConfig.Configure()` in the Application project —
as one `TypeAdapterConfig<Entity, Dto>.NewConfig()` line per mapping, grouped by feature.
Map **entity → DTO only**; Create/Update flow through the aggregate's `Create`/behavior methods,
not through mapping.

```csharp
// src/CoachApp.Application/CoachAppMapsterConfig.cs
public static class CoachAppMapsterConfig
{
    public static void Configure()
    {
        // ── Trainees ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        TypeAdapterConfig<Trainee, TraineeDto>.NewConfig();

        // ── TrainingPlans ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        TypeAdapterConfig<TrainingPlan, TrainingPlanDto>.NewConfig();
    }
}
```
Use `.Ignore(...)` for properties the AppService fills manually and
`.Map(dest => ..., src => ...)` for name/shape mismatches.

### Registration
`MapsterObjectMapper : IAutoObjectMappingProvider` routes ABP's `ObjectMapper` through Mapster.
`CoachAppApplicationModule` calls `CoachAppMapsterConfig.Configure()`, registers the config +
`IMapper`, and installs `MapsterObjectMapper` as the app's `IAutoObjectMappingProvider`.

### Usage in application service
```csharp
public virtual async Task<TraineeDto> GetAsync(Guid id)
{
    var trainee = await _traineeRepository.GetAsync(id);
    return ObjectMapper.Map<Trainee, TraineeDto>(trainee);        // single
    // ObjectMapper.Map<List<Trainee>, List<TraineeDto>>(list)    // list
}
```

> **Note**: Because mapping goes through `ObjectMapper`, services stay decoupled from the mapping
> library — only `CoachAppMapsterConfig` and the module registration know it is Mapster.
